## 13. Claude Code — install + headless auth for scheduled jobs

Not part of the original migration — added later to support the EOD
diagnostic/analysis pipeline (Steps 14–15). Optional if you're not using
those, but harmless to set up regardless.

```bash
curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash
echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.bashrc && source ~/.bashrc
claude --version
```

Then run `claude` interactively once to log in (Pro/Max/Team subscription, or
a Console API-billed account — the free claude.ai tier doesn't include Code
access). This is a **per-VPS, OAuth-based login** — it does not travel with
the repo or with `config_secrets.env`. **Must be redone on every new VPS.**

**Verify headless mode works before relying on it in cron** — interactive
login succeeding doesn't guarantee `-p` (non-interactive) mode authenticates
the same way; this is a known gotcha with OAuth-based sessions specifically:

```bash
claude -p "Reply with exactly: HEADLESS OK" --permission-mode auto --permission-prompts none
```

Expect `HEADLESS OK` printed directly. If this hangs or fails to authenticate
while interactive `claude` works fine, do not build cron jobs on top of it
until this specific check passes.

**Note:** official docs also mention a `--bare` flag as the recommended mode
for scripted/scheduled runs generally — **do not use it here.** `--bare` never
reads OAuth credentials and requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` instead, which breaks
a Pro/Max subscription login. Stick with `--permission-mode auto
--permission-prompts none` as shown above.

