## 14. Telegram bot for daily delivery

One-time setup, independent of any VPS — do this from a phone/browser, not
the VPS itself:

1. Telegram → message **@BotFather** → `/newbot` → follow prompts (pick a
   display name, then a username ending in `bot`) → save the API token it
   returns.
2. Message your new bot directly (anything, e.g. `/start`) — Telegram bots
   can't message you first, so this one-time message unlocks delivery.
3. Visit `https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates` (append a throwaway
   query param like `?x=1` if the browser caches a stale empty result) and
   read `"chat":{"id":...}` in the response — that number is the chat_id.

Add both to `config_secrets.env` alongside the 5 `ZERODHA_*` values (see
Step 5) — same file, same `chmod 600`, same "never commit" rule:

```bash
cat >> /root/paper/config_secrets.env << 'EOF'
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<token>
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=<chat_id>
EOF
```

Test delivery independent of any report code:
```bash
source /root/paper/config_secrets.env
curl -s "https://api.telegram.org/bot${TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN}/sendMessage" \
  -d "chat_id=${TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID}" -d "text=Test from VPS"
```

**The bot/token/chat_id are NOT tied to any specific VPS.** If migrating,
just copy these two values into the new `config_secrets.env` along with the
Zerodha ones — no need to create a new bot.

