## Pre-flight checklist

- [ ] `python3.11 --version` → 3.11.x
- [ ] venv points to it: `/root/paper/venv/bin/python3 --version`
- [ ] `nproc` → matches old VPS (stagger logic assumption in `run_daily_trackers.sh`)
- [ ] `config_secrets.env` present, `chmod 600`, login verified via `token.json`
- [ ] `ml_predictor/models/` has all 12 files after `train.py`
- [ ] `ml_predictor/run_daily_trackers.sh` is executable (`ls -l` shows `x` bits) — a fresh clone can lose this, and cron fails silently on `Permission denied` if missed
- [ ] `systemctl status algo` → clean manual start/stop, log shows full session
- [ ] `crontab -l` → matches, all Python lines use `venv/bin/python3`
- [ ] `run_daily_trackers.sh` internal `python3` call also uses venv path
- [ ] Fix pushed to GitHub (or at least committed locally) so next migration inherits it
- [ ] First live cron-triggered day watched manually via `tail -f trader.log`
- [ ] `.gitignore` actually working: `git check-ignore -v token.json config_secrets.env` prints a match for both
- [ ] Claude Code installed, logged in, AND headless mode verified (`claude -p "..." --permission-mode auto --permission-prompts none` prints output, doesn't hang) — only if using Steps 13-15
- [ ] Telegram bot token + chat_id in `config_secrets.env`, test message delivered — only if using Steps 14-15
- [ ] EOD analysis cron job present in `crontab -l`, uses full path `/root/.local/bin/claude` — only if using Step 15

